nodes.body:
Merged current main and pushed `8d73e32c48c3`. The new optional cache-hit-bound argument in `_get_local_prefix_cache_hit` made the forced-hit test double fail with a two-argument `TypeError`; this head forwards that argument through the double, preserving the original 16-token forced-hit setup. No production behavior was changed by that two-line adapter.

Validation on the merged head: the three reset/redo tests pass, all 56 completion-error tests pass, and full `test_scheduler.py` is 283 passed with only the known V1+PP async config-validation failure, which I reproduced identically on a separate bare-main snapshot. Pre-commit passes on the changed file. I also checked a clean combined snapshot with #60960: the same adapter issue appeared before the fix, and all 9 targeted tests pass after it. The PR description now separates that CPU compatibility result from the independent GPU evidence and explains which parts of #60960 overlap.

@Ondre119 the remaining decisive check is still your V1 async active-reset sweep, now against `8d73e32c48c3`. I have not rerun it on GPU and am not treating the CPU or CI results as a substitute. If you have time to repeat the same reproducer, the two exception shapes you measured should remain gone, and successful responses should still match the no-reset reference exactly.

